BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Plumbfinder) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: PLUMBFINDER) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Water damage inside homes is a large and growing problem in the United States. Alot of it comes) Tj T* (from slow hidden leaks that go on for weeks or months inside walls, under floors and under) Tj T* (slabs before anyone notices. By the time a homeowner sees a stain on the ceiling or gets an) Tj T* (unexpectedly high water bill, the damage is already done and the repair can be many thousands) Tj T* (of dollars. Older homes are hit the hardest because they still have original pipes, like) Tj T* (galvanized steel and old copper with soldered joints, that corrode and fail over time. There) Tj T* (are millions of such homes in the country and the owners are often on fixed budgets and do not) Tj T* (have a good way to know whats going on behind the drywall.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Today homeowners have two options and neither is good. They can wait and react when something) Tj T* (goes wrong, or they can pay a plumber or leak detection specialist who charges a few hundred) Tj T* (dollars per visit and only finds the problem if it is leaking at that moment. Existing smart) Tj T* (home leak sensors only tell you there is water on the floor, which is already too late, and) Tj T* (they do not tell you where the pipe is failing. Our team has talked to homeowners and many told) Tj T* (us they just feel anxious about it and do not know what to do.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Plumbfinder is a smart attachment for the water meter plus a mobile app. The attachment clips) Tj T* (onto the meter or the main supply line in a few minutes with no plumber and no cutting of) Tj T* (pipes. Inside it there is a sensor package that reads flow, pressure and vibration of the water) Tj T* (many times per second. The data goes by wifi to our cloud, where our analytics software looks) Tj T* (for the small patterns that show a leak, for example tiny flow at night when nobody is using) Tj T* (water or a specific vibration frequency from a pinhole in a pipe. The software then compares) Tj T* (the pattern to a library of leak signatures and gives a best guess of the zone of the house) Tj T* (where the failing pipe is, and how serious it is. The homeowner gets a notification on the app) Tj T* (that says something like probable slow leak in the bathroom supply line, medium urgency, and) Tj T* (can then call a plumber who knows where to look instead of tearing open walls.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We believe this approach is differentiated because it combines a physical product with data) Tj T* (analytics and gives location, not only a yes or no alarm. Our algorithms improve as we get more) Tj T* (homes in the system, which creates a data advantage over time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (According to public housing data, there are roughly 80 million homes in the US built before) Tj T* (1990, and we think a good share of them have pipe types at risk. We have not yet done a full) Tj T* (market sizing but as a rough estimate if even 5 percent of these homes adopted a product like) Tj T* (ours at around 150 dollars of hardware and 8 dollars per month, the market would be in the) Tj T* (billions. Our initial target is single family owner occupied homes built between 1940 and 1980) Tj T* (in cities with older housing stock and hard water, starting with our own region. Secondary) Tj T* (customers are landlords with small rental portfolios, home inspectors, and insurance companies) Tj T* (who pay out for water claims.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to make money in three ways. First, the hardware is sold direct to consumers at about) Tj T* (149 dollars, with a margin we estimate at 35 to 40 percent at current prototype costs, which) Tj T* (should improve with volume. Second, a monthly subscription of 7.99 dollars for the monitoring,) Tj T* (app and alerts, which gives recurring revenue. Third, in the future, partnerships with) Tj T* (insurance carriers who could subsidize devices or give premium discounts, and referral fees) Tj T* (from plumbers who get leads from our alerts. The insurance channel is the most promising but we) Tj T* (have only had early conversations and no agreements yet.) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
