BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are several competitors in the smart water space. Some companies sell whole home shutoff) Tj T* (valves that cut the water when a leak is detected, and others sell flow monitors that attach to) Tj T* (the main line. Basic leak sensor pucks are cheap and widely available. These are all good) Tj T* (products but in our understanding most of them focus on detecting that a leak exists or) Tj T* (stopping it, and not on telling the homeowner where the pipe is failing inside the house. Some) Tj T* (of them also require a plumber to install and cost much more. Our weakness is that we are) Tj T* (small, have no brand, and larger companies could add a location feature if they wanted to. Our) Tj T* (accuracy for locating leaks is also not yet proven at scale, which is our main technical risk.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Dariusz Kowalczyk is our CEO and is a senior in mechanical engineering, who led the design of) Tj T* (the hardware and the enclosure and has summer experience at a local manufacturing firm. Marisol) Tj T* (Okonkwo-Reyes is our CTO, a junior in computer science with a focus on machine learning, who) Tj T* (built the app and the leak detection software. Teague Brandvold is our head of business and is) Tj T* (a senior in business administration, who runs customer interviews, pricing and partnerships. We) Tj T* (also have an informal advisor, a retired plumbing contractor with 30 years of experience, who) Tj T* (has helped us understand real leak situations and who lets us test in homes he knows.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (To date we have built a working prototype of the attachment and a first version of the app, we) Tj T* (registered the company as an S Corp, and we have a website. We have placed units in 9 homes) Tj T* (owned by friends, family and neighbors of our advisor, and so far the system has flagged 3 leak) Tj T* (events, 2 of which were confirmed by a plumber and one was a false alarm. This is encouraging) Tj T* (but the sample is very small and we know it is not a real validation. We have spent about 6,500) Tj T* (dollars so far, mostly on parts, funded from our own savings and a small university grant. Our) Tj T* (current cost per unit is around 92 dollars in small batches. We expect in year one to sell) Tj T* (perhaps 800 units if we get a good channel, which would be about 120,000 dollars of hardware) Tj T* (revenue, plus subscription revenue that builds up during the year, but these are early) Tj T* (estimates and we do not have a full financial model yet.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for prize funding and support from this competition. Specifically we would use) Tj T* (funds to build a pilot batch of 100 units, improve the accuracy of our location algorithm) Tj T* (through testing in more homes with different pipe types, get the electronics tested for safety) Tj T* (certification, and hire a part time contractor to help with the cloud backend. Beyond the money) Tj T* (we would value mentorship, especially introductions to insurance industry contacts and advice) Tj T* (on how to set up our financial model and our pricing. We believe Plumbfinder can help many) Tj T* (homeowners avoid costly damage and we are excited to take the next step.) Tj ET
endstream
